      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters instead of dropping them, so `café` becomes `cafe`. All four tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. The old code skipped every non-ASCII letter. Now each letter is decomposed with Unicode NFKD and its ASCII base is kept, so accents are stripped. A small table covers letters that don't decompose, such as `ß` → `ss`, `ø` → `o`, `æ` → `ae`, `œ` → `oe`, `ł` → `l`, `đ`/`ð` → `d`, `þ` → `th`, and `ı` → `i`. Standalone combining marks are dropped rather than turned into dashes.\n\nI added two regression tests to `tests/test_core.py` covering `café`, `Ångström Crème`, `Straße` and `Øresund`.\n\nLetters with no ASCII equivalent, such as CJK characters, are still removed as before. I didn't change the existing behaviour that consecutive separators aren't collapsed.",
